From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: extcon: max77693: treat a charging downstream port as USB data

A CDP (e.g. a PC or hub port that also charges) only set
EXTCON_CHG_USB_CDP. The data lines were left unswitched and EXTCON_USB
never went high, so the USB controller, which takes VBUS from this MUIC
(0112), never started a peripheral session: no USB networking/gadget on
such ports, while an SDP worked. Handle a CDP like an SDP for the data
path and VBUS, keeping the CDP charger type for the current limits.

---
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-max77693.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-max77693.c
@@ -910,6 +910,16 @@
 		}
 		break;
 	case MAX77693_CHARGER_TYPE_DOWNSTREAM_PORT:
+		/*
+		 * A charging downstream port is a USB host port as well (PCs,
+		 * hubs): connect the data lines and report VBUS as for an SDP,
+		 * else the USB controller never starts a peripheral session.
+		 */
+		ret = max77693_muic_set_path(info, info->path_usb, attached);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+
+		extcon_set_state_sync(info->edev, EXTCON_USB, attached);
 		extcon_set_state_sync(info->edev, EXTCON_CHG_USB_CDP,
 					attached);
 		break;
